      "writtenOn": "2024-12-05T07:13:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No I think in the first case both would return 43, and in the second case both would return 42\n\nI think you\u0027d have something like:\n\n\n```\nif (stats \u003d\u003d null) {\n    // Cache miss, fetch from the service.\n    stats \u003d statsFetcher.get();\n\n    // Update the cache with the fetched result if valid.\n    if (stats !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 !isEmpty(stats)) {\n        final StatsResult cachedValue \u003d cache.putIfAbsent(key, stats);\n        if (cachedValue !\u003d null) {\n            // Some other thread cached a value after this thread originally got a cache miss.\n            // Return the cached value to ensure all returned values after caching are consistent.\n            return cachedValue;\n        }\n    }\n    return stats;\n}\n```\n\nBasically this ensures that if a value is put in cache, this will be the value returned by any thread as long as the cache is valid.",
